"Inbox_update_21_5_body" = "<b>Greetings, Adventurers!</b>\n\nThe 0.21.5 update is here with new Seasonal Quests, events, and more!\n\n◆ <b>The Season of Passage Continues</b>\nNew lessons await as the fourth and fifth Seasonal Quests approach. In the fields of Daylight Prairie and the farther reaches of Hidden Forest, the final passages welcome you in the remaining weeks of the Season. \n\nAs you progress, be sure to check in with the Passage Guide in Isle of Dawn to unlock the next quests—not to mention masks or even a prop for a new game to share.\n\nAll Seasonal Quests can be completed independently, though the value of each lesson is best experienced with completed with groups of other Sky Children. All quests except the first one are each held at set intervals several times per hour. You can gather in advance with others during the countdown to its starting time.\n\nSeason of Passage continues until 23:59 June 25th (all times PDT, UTC -7). Content can be enjoyed by all players who have progressed to at least Hidden Forest. \n\nPlayers with a Season Pass will also have the opportunity to unlock all items from the Seasonal Spirits and the Ultimate Gifts available through the Season of Passage Guide.\n\n\n◆ <b>Event-Specific Currencies</b>\nTo make it easier for players of all experience levels to unlock new items during the event, no matter how long they’ve played Sky, we’re introducing currencies that are used for each specific event. \n\nThese will make it possible to unlock mementos just by playing during an event, without having to choose to between using Candles for a new event item or something else.\n\nOut in the levels, event currencies vary in appearance to fit the theme of their event. In your inventory, they'll appear as a ticket with an event-related symbol on it. \n\nEvent currencies have some similarities to Seasonal Candles. \nFor example:\n● They’re available only for their event, and can be used to unlock those event's items—in this case, in-game currency items that are new this year. \n● Currencies won’t carry over from one event to another, but enough are available during an event to unlock the new in-game currency items.\n● You won’t need to play every day to get the amount needed to unlock said items.\n● Currencies won’t roll over from one event to the next.\n● Currencies are located in set locations each day, and the locations will rotate.\n\nHowever, event currencies have some <b>differences</b> compared to Seasonal Candles:\n※ At the end of an event, unused event currencies do <b>not</b> convert to Candles.\n※ From one event to another, there may be a different max number of event currency available each day.\n\nYou can find more details on our news page or in the 0.21.5 patch notes!\n\n\n◆ <b>Days of Color Brightens the Sky</b>\nFrom 00:00 May 29th until 23:59 June 11th, share new activities and memories with friends and fellow players. Building on the themes of Days of Rainbow, this expanded event returns with an updated name to keep rooting deeper into the message of hope and thriving inclusivity, celebrating the beauty that brightens our lives only when all colors can shine. \n\nIn Home two Spirits greet a double rainbow that offers Light to collect, and the ability to teleport to the area in Daylight Prairie where the festivities will be held!\n\nIn the event area, Spirits stand at one of eight colorful platforms. With each new day at the start of Days of Color, a platform awaits groups of players to bring the energy of their colors—and if you're needing a different color, step into the magical steam of the small geyser nearby to receive a spell that can help! \n\nEventually all 8 colors can be charged, and when they are, be prepared for a brilliant display that shares Light and lifts all players to glittering heights.\n\nDuring Days of Color, as you explore the event area and complete Daily Quests, keep an eye out for small colorful spheres to collect. These are the special event-themed currency you can use to unlock this year’s new free Days of Color cosmetic. \n\nSpecial charity IAP in the shop will aid real-world efforts to support diversity. In-game currency and IAP items from previous years of Days of Rainbow will also be available from event Spirits and the in-game shop. \n\nFor more information, see our patch notes or news post on thatskygame.com!\n\n\n◆ <b>New Harmonies of Days of Music</b>\nA cozy new event settles in from June 26th through July 9. Items to choose from, instruments to play, and even a little something to create ensemble recordings of your own...Stay tuned for more info as the event approaches!\n\n\nFor additional information, and to see some of the other bug fixes and updates in this patch, be sure to check the patch notes on our FAQ page. Access these by selecting “Support” in the Settings menu and choosing “Patch Notes.”\n\n\nSee you in the skies!\n\n\n~thatgamecompany";
